# Visual Refinement: Dashboard & Emission Pages

I have successfully updated the dashboard and emission calculation pages to create a more integrated, professional, and premium user experience.

## Key Changes

### 1. Professional SVG Integration
Replaced all dated emojis and external icon images with high-quality, professional inline SVGs. This ensures crisp rendering at any scale and a consistent visual language.

- **Dashboard**: "Data Entry" shortcuts now feature clean, themed SVGs instead of emojis.
- **Calculations**: Scope cards and source selectors now use unified SVG icons.
- **Specific Factors**: Source selection grid now features full-color SVG icons for Flaring, Venting, Mobile, and Stationary sources.

### 2. Design System Blending
Synchronized the design language across multiple pages to ensure a seamless transition for the user.

- **Sidebar & Top Bar**: Standardized across [dashboard.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.html), [emission-selection.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-selection.html), and [emission-factor.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-factor.html).
- **Glassmorphism**: Applied consistent background blur and transparency effects to calculation panels and cards.
- **Breadcrumbs**: Standardized navigation trails with professional icons and consistent spacing.

### 3. Page-Specific Improvements

#### [emission-factor.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-factor.html)
- Fully blended with the dashboard layout.
- Replaced emoji indicators with themed SVG icons.
- Modernized the "Calculate Factor" button with a professional SVG icon.

#### [emission-selection.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-selection.html)
- Replaced external Iconify images with permanent inline SVGs for better performance and consistency.
- Standardized action arrows.

## Screenshots / Results
The application now feels like a unified professional suite rather than a collection of separate tools.

